WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:14.969
“4, 3, 2, 1… 0!”

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:20.000
This is footage from the “Operation Ivy”
nuclear test in 1952.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.310
And this is a clip from the movie ‘Them!’

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:28.150
— a film released just two years later about
giant irradiated ants.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:34.550
And it wasn’t the only film from the Atomic
Age about mutant animals terrorizing the public.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:40.179
The pervasive fear of nuclear devastation
that haunted the Cold War would manifest on

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:44.539
screen as literal monsters time and time again.

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:50.519
We now understand that radiation is more likely
to poison animal life than to create Godzilla…

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:53.829
but what if that wasn’t the case?

00:00:53.829 --> 00:01:00.129
‘Barren,’ a post-apocalyptic worldbuilding
project by Keegan Francis, imagines an alternate

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:06.360
history where civilization ended in nuclear
conflict, and mutated animal life rapidly

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.400
evolves to rule over the irradiated wastes
left behind.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.670
A retro-future that calls to mind the worldbuilding
of the Fallout series, the project reveals

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:22.680
a world where human survivors must contend
with biological horrors created by their own

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.680
folly.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:29.780
So, for this entry into the archive, we’ll
travel across the wastes, creating a ‘survival

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.780
guide’ of sorts to the creatures that roam
this desolate world.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.300
And if you want to help support and build
this project, there’s a link to the artist’s

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.880
Patreon down below.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:47.250
Now, let’s cross into an alternate timeline,
and witness the broken world of Barren…

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:52.340
We’ll begin with the basics of mutant biology.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.010
In nature, animals change over time due to
random genetic mutations allowing certain

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:02.860
members of a species to better adapt to their
environment and pass on their genes.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:09.000
The irradiated environments of Barren speeds
up the rate of these mutations considerably.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.950
As a result, animals in this alternate timeline
now evolve to fill new niches with alarming

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:15.950
speed.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:21.969
Just a few generations after the world’s
end, most species of animals now look unrecognizable

00:02:21.969 --> 00:02:24.920
compared to their prewar ancestors.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:31.410
With evolution sent into overdrive, many familiar
species will die out in this new kingdom of

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.010
fierce competition.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:39.200
Beyond ambient fallout, the most extreme mutations
are brought on by an irradiated strain of

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:45.890
illness called Nukrosis — which subjects
its host to even more rapid evolutionary changes.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:53.299
While the disease often results in advantageous
mutations, it simultaneously reduces the host’s

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:56.470
lifespan — making it more of a curse than
a blessing.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:02.389
The Nukrosis infection has become a widespread
issue in various regions, contaminating a

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:06.939
significant percentage of the postwar biosphere.

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:11.749
The region we’ll be exploring in this video
was once the United Kingdom.

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:17.549
Yet the green landscapes of old have been
replaced by a grim wasteland of silent decay.

00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:23.079
The people’s spirit remains hopeful, however,
resulting in the region’s nickname: “The

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:24.760
Unbroken Kingdom.”

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:30.060
For among the small pockets of survivors,
hope is the last defense against the dangers

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.150
of the new world…

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:38.549
In the new reality of the Unbroken Kingdom,
farms of old no longer exist — with most

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:43.309
domesticated animals unable to survive in
the merciless new paradigm.

00:03:43.309 --> 00:03:47.400
Instead, new animals have assumed the role
of livestock in the settlements that have

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.419
risen from the ashes.

00:03:49.419 --> 00:03:54.871
The mighty Bulwark are a widespread species
of farm animal that are quite docile, despite

00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:57.870
what their horns and tusks might suggest.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.319
These mammals are related to prewar cows,
namely the Holstein Friesian (hol-steen free-zhen)

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:05.069
and Highland cattle breeds.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:10.750
With adults known to weigh well over a ton,
Bulwark are classified as megafauna, and have

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.900
the tenacity needed to endure the unforgiving
postwar reality.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.769
Taking a closer look at the Bulwark’s hide,
we can see that their thick, leathery skin

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.300
acts as a kind of natural body armor.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:28.630
While they retain the familiar pattern of
their bovine ancestors, the Bulwark’s protective

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:32.660
hide is closer to that of an Old-World rhino.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:38.910
Postwar farmers rear Bulwarks on the fertile
fields around a region called “New Yorkshire”

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:44.160
— making the area one of the more prosperous
in the Unbroken Kingdom...

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.670
Yet Bulwarks aren’t the only new farm animal
found within the meager settlements of the

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:50.670
Kingdom.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.780
The uncanny Bonehens are a common sight in
this new world.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.521
Their cretaceous-esque features make them
well adapted to the harsh environment, with

00:04:59.521 --> 00:05:04.150
the bonehen’s spikes helping them stay cool
during heatwaves.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.470
Bonehens serve as the replacement for the
chickens of the old world — and have changed

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.120
much from their tame predecessors.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:17.000
Their beak is deceptively strong, designed
to crush eggshells and other discarded scraps

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.750
for an easy source of protein.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:24.700
Comparing a Bonehen’s feathers to the plumage
of an old-world chicken, it becomes clear

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.350
that the Bonehen’s feathers are significantly
fused and matted.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:34.280
Their makeup is almost more akin to the hardened
scales of a reptile than the soft plumage

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.590
of a bird.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:41.620
Due to a shortage of food, the surviving government
has released posters urging civilians to rear

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.310
Bonehens as a source of sustenance.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:50.020
While eating a mutated species like a Bonehen
is a viable means of staying alive in desperate

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:56.190
times, the long-term effects of consuming
such meals remain to be seen...

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:01.650
Just beyond the fences, far more dangerous
lifeforms prowl the ruined countryside.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:07.920
In some regions of the Unbroken Kingdom, hazard
signs warn travelers to stay clear of nearby

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.690
Zadger nests.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:15.220
Mid-sized predators, the Zadgers are a well-known
threat found all across the former British

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.300
Isles.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:21.420
With bone-crushing jaws and a poisonous barb
on the end of their tail, Zadgers are the

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:25.780
bane of unwary travelers who stray too far
from the path.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:31.870
Yet surprisingly, these deadly animals are
the descendants of the harmless prewar badger,

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.750
which grew in size and ferocity to adapt to
an unforgiving world.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:42.560
Modern Zadgers are almost entirely hairless,
giving them a wrinkled appearance.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.870
Closer analysis of their glabrous (glay-brus)
skin indicates their baldness is likely due

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:51.950
to an amino acid substitution in a hair growth
associated protein.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:58.580
An analogous prewar mutation had occurred
in naked mole rats, resulting in their characteristic

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:04.680
lack of visible fur; while unsettling in appearance,
the mole rats were not dangerous.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:10.770
But in this world, with creatures like Zadgers
on the prowl, roaming the wilds can be a serious

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.150
mistake.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.950
And more frightening things than Zadgers have
evolved in the Unbroken Kingdom.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:23.310
For woodland animals aren’t the only things
that have been mutated in the new world.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.240
Some humans have been changed as well, transforming
into a new species of predators.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:32.660
Characterized by their long frame, claws,
and almost vampiric features, these dark reflections

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:38.660
of humanity — known as the Nukula — haunt
the barren wastes like vengeful ghosts.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:44.350
The Nukula can vary in many ways — with
most being frail and sickly, forcing them

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.180
to become ambush predators.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:52.960
These slow Nukula hide in ruins of pre-war
buildings, feeding on explorers who delve

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.110
too deep.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:59.740
For the Nukulas still possess their human
intelligence, able to set traps to lure and

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.330
ensnare their unlucky victims.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:08.810
And in other parts of the Unbroken Kingdom,
rarer and more dangerous variants of Nukula

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.500
have emerged.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:14.610
Fearsome Nukula are faster and bulkier than
their slow relatives.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:20.360
Unlike their smaller counterparts, Fearsome
Nukula are roaming predators as opposed to

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.120
their scavenger cousins.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:27.889
As a consequence of this lifestyle, the arms
of Fearsome Nukula have become larger and

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:34.570
more heavily muscled — and their hands now
end in grasping talons used to ensnare prey.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:39.120
Their jaws and teeth have also evolved — and
are now strong enough to break through the

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.150
hides of the tenacious animals that roam the
countryside.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:50.000
Analysis suggests the Fearsome Nukula’s
extreme mutations come from the Nukrosis disease.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:56.010
While Nukrosis makes them apex predators,
the illness also shortens their lifespan — meaning

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:59.720
their numbers are few…

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.960
A more common lifeform can be found a bit
closer to the ground.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:10.090
Dillo-pigs are animals that prove not all
organisms in this new age are quite so frightening.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:16.410
A pervasive species capable of reproducing
quickly, these animals are often found on

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.440
the outskirts of settlements.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:24.540
Like prewar rodents, Dillo-Pigs proliferate
in large numbers, and are quite adept at scavenging

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.600
for food.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.150
Unlike most prewar rodents, however, Dillo-Pigs
have evolved thick armor plating on their

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:34.529
backs to shield against the predators of the
wastes.

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:40.100
These hardened scales resemble the protective
leathery shell of old-world armadillo species

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.200
— from which the Dillo-Pigs get their nickname.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:49.340
Dillo-Pigs are also known to create concealed
nests within prewar ruins, which they retreat

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.050
into when threats arise.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:56.810
And with thousands of miles of abandoned piping
still present underground, Dillo-Pigs have

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.470
plenty of room to make their burrows.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:04.580
Thankfully, the Dillo-Pig is one of the few
animals left in the world that could be considered

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:11.290
pet-like due to their harmless nature and
relatively cute appearance.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:16.540
Those who make their homes in the ruins of
urban areas must deal with other types of

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.610
animals.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:22.880
Goldwings are a species of city-dwelling bat
associated with the growing region of New

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.500
Yorkshire.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:29.500
Despite their somewhat startling appearance,
Goldwings aren’t aggressive towards humans.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:35.960
The descendants of prewar bats, they feed
primarily on insects and other small organisms.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:41.460
Their name comes from the golden hue of their
vibrant wings, which might serve as camouflage

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.330
against the ambient light of cities.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:49.640
Most Goldwings hunt by hanging off lampposts
and staying completely still, waiting for

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:54.230
pests to run into the open — only to end
up as an easy meal.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:59.180
Because Goldwings feed on disease-carrying
pests, they’ve been marked as an asset by

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:04.529
the government of the Unbroken Kingdom, and
are considered a protected species.

00:11:04.529 --> 00:11:09.720
As a result, the hunting of any Goldwings
within the limits of New Yorkshire will earn

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:14.220
offenders a hefty fine…

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:20.420
Just beyond the outer limits of urban areas,
scavengers lurk on the edges of civilization.

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.890
The Rotfowl are massive birds that stand taller
than a person, and feed on any carcass that

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:31.510
come their way — no matter how rotten…
or how fresh.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:36.920
Often seen feasting upon remains from local
skirmishes, they have earned the nickname

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.750
‘birds of war.’

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:44.529
The descendent of a pre-war bird of prey,
the Rotfowl have become larger and more terrestrial

00:11:44.529 --> 00:11:50.370
than their ancestors — having converged
upon a towering body plan similar to the fearsome

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:53.120
Cassowaries of the old world.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:57.899
To match their unpleasant diet, their beaks
have become sharp and hook-like.

00:11:57.899 --> 00:12:03.500
Yet Rotfowl actually play a key role in decomposition
within their environment.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:08.620
Like vultures, the function they serve within
the food web might be unglamorous, yet it

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.590
is fundamental to various ecosystems.

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:15.720
For Rotfowl don’t just affect the health
of the Unbroken Kingdom.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:21.200
Studies of their migratory patterns indicate
that Rotfowl travel across the North Sea once

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:29.040
a year, roaming in large groups to other lands
during the height of their mating season.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:34.440
Genetic mutations are responsible for most
of the fauna found across the Unbroken Kingdom.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:40.100
Yet the greatest horrors of the wastes are
in fact the result of prewar experiments conducted

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.640
by a company called Biophage.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:49.380
A clandestine organization with a long history
of ethical and moral violations, their story

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:52.640
begins long before the war started.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:58.200
Originally formed as a pharmaceutical corporation,
the company found its sales began to falter

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.110
over the decades.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:06.750
Everything changed, however, when Biophage
was taken over by one Dr. Ellingham, a successful

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:13.520
businessman with no background in biology…
and no intention of engaging in ethical science.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:19.060
Under his leadership, Biophage pivoted to
become a company on the cutting edge of prewar

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.740
bio-engineering.

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:26.130
The exact nature of the early prewar company
experiments is largely unknown.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:32.540
And perhaps that is for the best, for what
we do have on record is bone-chilling…

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:39.540
Not long before the outbreak of the war, Biophage,
under the oversight of Dr. Ellingham, began

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:42.380
experimenting with medical rejuvenation.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:46.550
Unit 1-51 would be one of these many attempts.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:51.060
Nicknamed ‘Ankle Biters,’ some of these
experiments could be considered technically

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:56.130
successful, as the Ankle Biters were able
to regrow lost limbs as intended.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:01.300
Yet the result were lifeforms that could no
longer be considered human.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:06.660
Still, Biophage might have increased the scale
of these experiments were it not for the violent

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.610
collapse of prewar society.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:13.180
Yet not all experiments were destroyed during
the war.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:18.230
Some creations of Biophage escaped into the
barren waste — and have been able to carve

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:22.440
out a niche in the brutal new natural hierarchy.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:29.330
Today, perhaps no lifeform in the Unbroken
Kingdom is more dangerous than the seldom-seen

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:33.930
Biophage experiment that stalks the open plains.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:40.050
Vespores are ruthless bioweapons capable of
horrors far beyond any naturally-evolved form

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.230
of life.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:46.779
While the original intention behind their
creation remains unknown, the results of the

00:14:46.779 --> 00:14:49.430
experiment are visible to all.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:55.080
Vespores hunt with a stinger-like appendage
capable of spearing fast-moving prey.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:01.420
Once an animal has been speared, the Vespore
then prepares to digest the unlucky creature.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:06.869
The internal anatomy of a Vespore allows them
to digest prey directly through their abdomen

00:15:06.869 --> 00:15:12.580
— making them extremely efficient, as they
are able to feast while on the move.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:18.120
The terrifying behavior of the Vespore coupled
with its elusive nature has caused it to take

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:22.830
on an almost mythical status in the minds
of some survivors.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:29.130
For not many see a Vespore and live to tell
the tale…

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:35.140
Aside from terrifying monsters, there is a
quiet sadness that the world of Barren evokes.

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:40.720
It is hard not to read through the project
and feel a certain melancholy for all that

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.060
has been lost.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.779
Bustling towns.

00:15:43.779 --> 00:15:45.260
Healthy forests.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:46.590
Clean rivers.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:51.580
Much of the world as it existed before the
apocalypse has changed utterly, and might

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.769
never return to normal.

00:15:53.769 --> 00:15:58.520
Yet the people of this alternate timeline
have adapted to the changes, much like the

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.019
strange fauna that now roam the wilderness.

00:16:02.019 --> 00:16:08.390
The Unbroken Kingdom might be an unfamiliar
landscape, but so long as its people continue

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:11.700
to endure, it will never be a broken one.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:16.670
There’s much more to the ‘Barren’ project
than I was able to cover in this video.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:20.750
If you want to see more from the world of
‘Barren,’ you can support Keegan Francis

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:26.590
on his Patreon down below, to access bonus
content and help the project continue.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:31.240
And as always, thanks for watching.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:36.290
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:41.080
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:50.250
See you in the next video.

